  "reviewedFrom": "Standard accrual year-end practice: every income-statement account (income, cost of sales, expense — custom accounts included) is closed to retained earnings at the fiscal year end; balance-sheet accounts, owner contributions and owner distributions are never closed. Net income = income − cost of sales − expense for the fiscal year; RE(end) = RE(open) + net income. A reopened year recloses only the residual change. Statements for a closed year still report its earnings (closing entries are excluded from the P&L). Pending licensed-CPA review (B16.3). Amounts are integer cents. Cash-side accounts are a non-control escrow asset (1060) so the year end is isolated from bank reconciliation, which BANK-01 covers.",
